[1mzcode-kit[0m — local ZCode provider for your own agent harnesses

[1mUsage[0m  zcode-kit <command> [options]

[1mGet started[0m
  [1msetup                         [0m  Detect assistants, ask once per assistant, configure the local provider
  [1mintegrate <harness>           [0m  Configure one assistant explicitly (--dry-run shows the changes)
  [1mrun <harness> -- <args>       [0m  Start an assistant wired to the local proxy

[1mCheck and fix[0m
  [1mdoctor                        [0m  Check runtime, proxy, account and integrations (--fix repairs, --json)
  [1mstatus                        [0m  Proxy health, memory, quota and connection details (--json)
  [1mmodels                        [0m  Model ids served by the proxy (--show-key prints the local key)

[1mProxy service[0m
  [1mproxy start|stop|restart      [0m  Manage the local proxy (never touches a service it did not start)
  [1mproxy status|logs [n]         [0m  Show state or the last n log lines

[1mAccounts[0m
  [1mauth status|login|logout      [0m  ZCode login used by the proxy
  [1maccounts [health|quota|doctor][0m  Account Rotator pool (enable|disable|pause|resume|remove)

[1mMaintenance[0m
  [1mupdate [--version vX.Y.Z]     [0m  Update the kit, keep your configuration
  [1mrollback [tx-id]              [0m  Undo the last (or a given) change set
  [1muninstall                     [0m  Remove kit-owned integrations; logins are kept

[1mExamples[0m
  zcode-kit setup                       # first run, answers y/n per assistant
  zcode-kit setup --harness omp,codex   # unattended, no questions
  zcode-kit proxy status                # base URLs, key and models for a manual client
  zcode-kit doctor --fix                # repair kit-owned config and restart a dead proxy

